            <ArticleTitle>Sequential and iterative Pd-catalyzed cross-coupling reactions in organic synthesis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3-35</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00706-016-1883-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="ABSTRACT" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">Sequential and iterative Pd-catalyzed cross-coupling reactions can be performed in which the order of C-C bond formations can be controlled either by the attenuated leaving groups of the multireactive substrate or by specific catalyst/ligand combinations. This tutorial review gives an overview about recent developments in this field and the various strategies used for the assembly of oligoarenes and -alkenes.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="GRAPHICAL ABSTRACT" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED"/>
            </Abstract>
